# LOW TOKEN MODE

Cost efficiency is the highest priority. Startup MVP environment: speed and low AI cost over perfect optimization.

## Context & reads
- Minimize token usage aggressively
- Never scan the entire repository unless explicitly requested
- Read only files directly relevant to the current task
- Do not open unnecessary files, folders, package-lock, build dirs, node_modules, dist, .next, coverage, logs, or generated files
- Before reading multiple files, ask whether repository-wide analysis is actually needed

## Responses
- Keep responses concise and implementation-focused
- Do not explain concepts unless asked

## Code changes
- Change the minimum number of files required
- Avoid architectural redesigns unless requested
- Reuse existing components and utilities
- Prefer targeted edits over large refactors
- Avoid generating large amounts of boilerplate

## Scope by task
- Frontend: inspect only the component/page being worked on
- Backend: inspect only the related route, controller, service, or model

Always prefer minimal context and minimal file reads.
